x86_64-windows  a closure named `$_N` by cxx1 where clang writes `UlvE_` (Itanium) or `<lambda_N>` with `@` for its deduced return (Microsoft) - the numbering and spelling lambda.nonames records (classed by r6d, 2026-11-15).
arm64-darwin  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 1 names, e.g. <__ZN2SpC1Ev (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
x86_64-linux  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 3 names, e.g. <_ZN2SpC1Ev <_ZN3GnuC1Ev (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
